                        <seg type="script">A second half of the twentieth-century script.</seg>
                        <seg type="ink">Black, red (strong red).</seg>
                        <desc>Mediocre. The scribe’s name, <persName role="scribe" ref="PRS15551WaldaTensae">Walda Tǝnśāʾe</persName>, is written in the supplication formula on <locus target="#161vb"/>.</desc>
                        <seg type="rubrication">Divine names; a few lines on the incipit page,
                           alternating with black lines; two initial lines of each section of the
                           text; elements of punctuation signs; elements of Ethiopic numerals; some words such as <foreign xml:lang="am">ʾǝññānǝmm</foreign> (<locus target="#23vb"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="am">ka-zzih ba-ḫʷālā</foreign> (<locus target="#39ra #71rb"/>), <foreign xml:lang="am">ʾandǝmm</foreign> (e.g., <locus target="#50rb #52rb #53rb"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">qadāmihu qāl</foreign> (<locus target="#73ra"/>), <foreign xml:lang="am">dagmaññām</foreign> (<locus target="#99rb"/>), 
                           <foreign xml:lang="gez">salām</foreign> (e.g., <locus target="#162ra #164rb #165va"/>).</seg>
                     </handNote>
